@* Description list (UI docs). Sections: Usage, Examples, Customization, Styling reference, API, Accessibility, Guidelines. *@

<ul class="dnf-docs-source">
    <li>CSS <code>src/DotNetForge.UI/Styles/components/content.css</code></li>
</ul>

<h2 id="usage">Usage</h2>
<p>A description list shows label and value pairs on ruled rows - the read-only details of a record, or system
    information. It is a real <code>&lt;dl&gt;</code> with one <code>&lt;dd&gt;</code> per <code>&lt;dt&gt;</code>, usually in a
    card body.</p>

<ui-doc-example id="basic" layout="block">
    <dl class="dnf-description-list">
        <dt>Status</dt>
        <dd><dnf-badge tone="Success" dot="true">Enabled</dnf-badge></dd>
        <dt>Version</dt>
        <dd><code>1.4.0</code></dd>
        <dt>Author</dt>
        <dd>DotNetForge</dd>
    </dl>
</ui-doc-example>

<h2 id="examples">Examples</h2>

<ui-doc-example id="compact" title="Compact" description="dnf-description-list--compact makes the label column as wide as its longest label and the rows tighter - for short facts in a side panel." layout="block">
    <dl class="dnf-description-list dnf-description-list--compact">
        <dt>Type</dt>
        <dd>image/jpeg</dd>
        <dt>Size</dt>
        <dd>1.2 MB</dd>
        <dt>Dimensions</dt>
        <dd>2400 × 1600</dd>
    </dl>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-example id="in-a-card" title="In a card" description="Values can hold any inline content: a link, a timestamp, a badge, code." layout="block">
    <section class="dnf-card">
        <div class="dnf-card__header">
            <h3 class="dnf-card__title">Webhook</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="dnf-card__body">
            <dl class="dnf-description-list">
                <dt>URL</dt>
                <dd><a href="#in-a-card">https://hooks.example.com/cms</a></dd>
                <dt>Events</dt>
                <dd><code>entry.published</code>, <code>media.uploaded</code></dd>
                <dt>Created</dt>
                <dd><dnf-timestamp value="new DateTime(2026, 1, 15, 9, 30, 0, DateTimeKind.Utc)" absolute="true" /></dd>
                <dt>Last delivery</dt>
                <dd><dnf-badge tone="Danger" class="dnf-badge--mono">500</dnf-badge></dd>
            </dl>
        </div>
    </section>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-example id="long-values" title="Long values" description="A value breaks anywhere when it must, so long URLs, ids and hashes never widen the page." layout="block">
    <dl class="dnf-description-list">
        <dt>Signing secret id</dt>
        <dd>whsec_7f3a9c2e4b1d8f6a0c5e3b9d7f1a2c4e6b8d0f3a5c7e9b1d</dd>
        <dt>Storage path</dt>
        <dd>media/2026/10/originals/a-very-long-file-name-that-keeps-going-and-going.jpg</dd>
    </dl>
</ui-doc-example>

<h2 id="customization">Customization</h2>
<p>The three <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/customization">customization levels</a>, none needing <code>!important</code>.</p>

<ui-doc-example id="custom-tailwind" title="Tailwind utilities" description="Utilities on a dd or dt style one value or label." layout="block">
    <dl class="dnf-description-list">
        <dt>Commit</dt>
        <dd class="font-mono">1354641</dd>
        <dt class="font-semibold">Environment</dt>
        <dd>Production</dd>
    </dl>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-example id="custom-css" title="Your own CSS" description="The description list has no component tokens; restyle it in a scope with your own (unlayered) CSS - here a narrow label column." layout="block">
    <div class="dnf-docs-demo-details">
        <dl class="dnf-description-list">
            <dt>Host</dt>
            <dd>localhost:5432</dd>
            <dt>Database</dt>
            <dd>PostgreSQL 17</dd>
        </dl>
    </div>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-code id="custom-css-code" lang="css">
.dnf-docs-demo-details .dnf-description-list {
    grid-template-columns: 6rem 1fr;
}
</ui-doc-code>

<h2 id="styling">Styling reference</h2>
<h3 id="classes">Classes</h3>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Class</th><th>Kind</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-description-list</code></td><td>block</td><td>a two-column grid: labels 8-12rem, values the rest; each <code>dt</code> and <code>dd</code> padded with a line below (none on the last pair)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-description-list--compact</code></td><td>modifier</td><td>the label column as wide as its longest label, less padding</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-description-list &gt; dt</code></td><td>-</td><td>muted</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-description-list &gt; dd</code></td><td>-</td><td>wraps anywhere (long URLs, ids)</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 id="api">API</h2>
<p>The description list has no tag helper: the classes above are its API, on a <code>&lt;dl&gt;</code> whose children are
    <code>&lt;dt&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;dd&gt;</code> pairs.</p>

<h2 id="accessibility">Accessibility</h2>
<ul>
    <li>A real <code>&lt;dl&gt;</code>: screen readers announce the pairs and their number.</li>
    <li>Keep exactly one <code>dd</code> per <code>dt</code> - the grid lays them out in pairs.</li>
    <li>Don't wrap pairs in <code>&lt;div&gt;</code>s; the grid expects <code>dt</code> and <code>dd</code> as direct children.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="guidelines">Guidelines</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Do use it inside a card body for read-only details.</li>
    <li>Do keep labels short; values can be long.</li>
    <li>Don't use it for editable fields - use a <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/components/form">form</a>.</li>
    <li>Don't use it for many records with the same fields - use a <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/components/table">table</a>.</li>
</ul>
